# SPA fallback — fixes "404 on refresh / direct link".
#
# Netlify serves this folder as static files. A route such as /settings or
# /developer-settings has no matching file on disk, so Netlify returns its own
# 404 page. This rule serves index.html (with a 200, not a 301) for every
# unmatched path, letting the React router take over.
#
# Why this file in addition to netlify.toml: everything in public/ is copied
# into the build output (dist/ or build/). That means the rule still works if
# the folder is uploaded to Netlify manually, or if the site's build settings
# were overridden in the Netlify UI — neither of which uses netlify.toml.
#
# Keep this rule LAST so real files win.

/*    /index.html   200
